<title>SWEDEN: Volvo deputy CEO to retire after 21 yrs.</title>
<headline>Volvo deputy CEO to retire after 21 yrs.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker AB Volvo said on Friday that its deputy chief executive officer Sten Langenius was to retire on June 30 after 21 years with the company.</p>
<p>Langenius was chief executive of Volvo Truck for 18 years, Volvo said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
